    "subtype": "success",
    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "The fix is ready! Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## The Problem\nWhen running `frai gate init --ci`, the `--ci` flag wasn't being passed to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI because Commander.js was consuming it at the parent program level. This caused the workflow file (`.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`) not to be created.\n\n## The Solution\nI added `.passThroughOptions()` to the `gate` command definition (packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts:741). This tells Commander.js to pass through options that come after the subcommand, rather than parsing them at the parent level.\n\n## The Change\n```typescript\nprogram\n  .command('gate [args...]')\n  .description('Responsible AI Gate for specs: init | check <spec> [--smart] | draft. Delegates to frai-gate.')\n  .allowUnknownOption(true)\n  .passThroughOptions()  // \u2190 Added this line\n  .helpOption(false)\n```\n\nNow when users run `frai gate init --ci`, the `--ci` flag will be passed through to `frai-gate`, which will correctly create both FRAI-SPEC.md and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`.",
